"building with `clang` on Linux, one should follow a recipe like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../overlay_mode.md:96
msgid ""
"If you installed `libllvmlibc.a` in a standard linker lookup path, for "
"example `/usr/local/lib` on Linux like systems, then specifying the path to "
"the static archive using the `-L` option is not necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../overlay_mode.md:100
msgid "Linking the static archive to other LLVM binaries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../overlay_mode.md:102
msgid ""
"Since the libc and other LLVM binaries are developed in the same source "
"tree, linking `libllvmlibc.a` to those LLVM binaries does not require any "
"special install step or explicitly passing any special linker flags/options. "
